YANI for Catnip: Represented by % of whatever colour RL catnip is.
Generated in with much the same probability/ in the same sort of
places as wolvesbane or garlic.

For the purposes of this post, "cats" refer to any f monster or
were-f, for example weretigers & werepanthers in either their f or @
form. (Are were-f slashem-specific? I can't remember)

Cats would be drawn to catnip and would follow it everywhere. Once a
cat gets within a square of some catnip (or within a square of a
player/ monster carrying catnip in main inventory) it starts acting
wierdly: Rolling around purring, staggering about as if stunned,
biting the player / nearby monsters at random, chewing and shredding
items on the floor.

Once a cat finds some catnip they won't leave it alone for anything,
which is great for distracting hostiles but a real pain in the tail if
your pet kitten gets a herbal habit and loses all interest in you. If
your kitty does get stuck on some 'nip, the best you can do is pick up
the catnip (in which case the cat will follow you around, but be
completely uninterested in fighting/ shoplifting for you) or hide it/
dispose of it somewhere: hide it in a container, bury it in a pit,
kick it into some water etc.

You could dispose of it by eating it, but this gives the catnip effect
as a permanent intrinsic- cats will follow the player about and then
behave strangely as soon as they catch up. A quick google-search seems
to indicate that eating catnip is not harmful to humans in RL, so
there needn't be any other effects. Maybe another new item (sprig of
dogwort?) could be introduced to remove the catnip intrinsic.

If a player polymorphs into a f or were-f, (s)he gets stunned and
confused in the presence of catnip. Eating it in this form will cure
the stunning and confusion, but cause a few hundred turns of
hallucination instead. It will also cure any kind of feline
lycanthropy, leaving the player in the f form rather than the @.

All catnip-induced hallucinations are characters and objects from
cat-related fiction and lore (Garfield, Thundercats, Tailchaser's
Song, you get the idea) and can be removed by any of the usual
hallucination-curing methods or by polymorphing into a non-cat form.

